{
  "title": "Cambridge's tap water comes from under the ground",
  "voice": "bm_george",
  "speed": 1.05,
  "lead_in": 0.1,
  "hook": [
    "CAMBRIDGE'S WATER",
    "COMES FROM UNDERGROUND"
  ],
  "lines": [
    {
      "text": "Cambridge's tap water comes from underground.",
      "gap": 0.3,
      "caps": [
        "*CAMBRIDGE'S WATER",
        "FROM *UNDERGROUND"
      ],
      "scene": {
        "type": "map",
        "cam": [
          0.12,
          52.2,
          9000
        ],
        "pins": [
          [
            "CAMBRIDGE",
            0.12,
            52.2,
            null
          ]
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Ninety-nine per cent of its supply is groundwater.",
      "gap": 0.3,
      "caps": [
        "*99 PER CENT",
        "IS *GROUNDWATER"
      ],
      "scene": {
        "type": "stat",
        "tag": "OFFICIAL · GOV.UK",
        "items": [
          {
            "v": "99",
            "suffix": "%",
            "l": "CAMBRIDGE WATER · FROM GROUNDWATER",
            "red": true
          }
        ],
        "bars": true,
        "source": "GOV.UK, MARCH 2024"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Not a river. Not a reservoir. Rock.",
      "gap": 0.3,
      "caps": [
        "NOT A *RIVER",
        "NOT A *RESERVOIR",
        "*ROCK"
      ],
      "scene": {
        "type": "icon",
        "icon": "rock",
        "title": "THE CHALK AQUIFER",
        "label": "WATER STORED IN ROCK"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "It's held in the chalk aquifer, south and east of the city.",
      "gap": 0.3,
      "caps": [
        "THE *CHALK AQUIFER",
        "SOUTH AND *EAST"
      ],
      "scene": {
        "type": "map",
        "cam": [
          0.3,
          52.1,
          12000
        ],
        "pins": [
          [
            "CAMBRIDGE",
            0.12,
            52.2,
            null
          ]
        ],
        "hatch": "southeast",
        "hatchLabel": "CHALK",
        "hatchLabelAt": [
          0.7,
          51.85
        ],
        "title": "CAMBRIDGE · CHALK AQUIFER"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Cambridge Water pumps it up from twenty-four boreholes.",
      "gap": 0.3,
      "caps": [
        "PUMPED UP",
        "FROM *24 BOREHOLES"
      ],
      "scene": {
        "type": "stat",
        "tag": "OFFICIAL · CAMBRIDGE WATER",
        "items": [
          {
            "v": "24",
            "suffix": "",
            "l": "BOREHOLES",
            "red": true
          }
        ],
        "source": "CAMBRIDGE WATER"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Cambridge averages five hundred and eighty-five millimetres of rain a year.",
      "gap": 0.3,
      "caps": [
        "*585 MM",
        "OF RAIN",
        "A *YEAR"
      ],
      "scene": {
        "type": "stat",
        "tag": "OFFICIAL · CAMBRIDGE WATER",
        "items": [
          {
            "v": "585",
            "suffix": " mm",
            "l": "AVERAGE RAINFALL A YEAR",
            "red": true
          }
        ],
        "source": "CAMBRIDGE WATER"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "And half of it needs to fall in winter, to refill the chalk.",
      "gap": 0.3,
      "caps": [
        "*HALF OF IT",
        "IN *WINTER",
        "TO *REFILL IT"
      ],
      "scene": {
        "type": "card",
        "tag": "OFFICIAL · CAMBRIDGE WATER",
        "l1": "WINTER RAIN",
        "l2": "REFILLS THE CHALK",
        "source": "CAMBRIDGE WATER"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "That chalk also feeds chalk streams. About eighty-five per cent of the world's are in England.",
      "gap": 0.3,
      "caps": [
        "*CHALK STREAMS",
        "*85 PER CENT",
        "IN *ENGLAND"
      ],
      "scene": {
        "type": "stat",
        "tag": "OFFICIAL · CAMBRIDGE WATER",
        "items": [
          {
            "v": "85",
            "suffix": "%",
            "l": "WORLD'S CHALK STREAMS IN ENGLAND",
            "red": true
          }
        ],
        "bars": true,
        "source": "CAMBRIDGE WATER"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "A new Fens Reservoir is planned for the mid twenty-thirties.",
      "gap": 0.3,
      "caps": [
        "A NEW *FENS",
        "*RESERVOIR",
        "MID *2030s"
      ],
      "scene": {
        "type": "card",
        "tag": "OFFICIAL · GOV.UK",
        "l1": "FENS RESERVOIR",
        "l2": "EXPECTED 2035–37",
        "source": "GOV.UK, MARCH 2024"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "River, reservoir or ground? Comment your guess.",
      "gap": 0.2,
      "caps": [
        "RIVER, RESERVOIR",
        "OR *GROUND?",
        "COMMENT YOUR *GUESS"
      ],
      "scene": {
        "type": "cta",
        "title": "COMMENT YOUR GUESS"
      }
    }
  ],
  "sources": [
